{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe grounding worker harness hard-codes POSIX `fork`. CPython 3.12 warns when this runs in a multithreaded host because the child can deadlock; Python 3.14 no longer defaults to fork. Runtime experiments confirmed `multiprocessing/popen_fork.py -> os.fork()` is the warning source, while spawn preserves 46/47 existing lifecycle tests. The one failure is a test fixture that attaches an unpicklable local closure to a Process. No production caller exists in-repo, but `run_in_worker` is publicly re-exported.\n\n## Approved API contract\n- Default to the cross-platform `spawn` context.\n- Accept an optional caller-supplied multiprocessing context for informed legacy/frozen-executable compatibility; callers explicitly selecting fork own its thread-safety risk.\n- Require worker callables to be importable module-level names and args, kwargs, and return values to be pickleable. Future C-extension bindings construct parser/query state inside the child from plain-data arguments.\n- Preserve the documented never-raise/fail-open contract: process start and pickling failures, plus parent receive/unpickling failures, return an abstaining `RunResult`.\n- Do not add cloudpickle/loky without a demonstrated production caller requiring dynamic callables.\n\n## Plan\n- Add held-out behavioral coverage proving the default worker completes under a live background thread with the fork warning promoted to error.\n- Add contract coverage for explicit context injection and non-pickleable start/receive failures mapping to fail-open results.\n- Switch the default context to spawn, expose optional context injection, and make start/receive cleanup exception-safe.\n- Replace the spawn-incompatible reap-lag test mutation with a parent-only proxy while preserving the crash-vs-timeout oracle.\n- Document the public callable/serialization contract and explicit fork escape hatch.\n- Run the grounding lifecycle/conformance matrix, mutation checks, lint, typecheck, and repository gates.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Default `run_in_worker` completes under a live background thread with the fork deadlock warning treated as an error.\n- [ ] An explicitly supplied multiprocessing context is used.\n- [ ] Non-importable or non-pickleable worker inputs return `RunResult(abstain_reason=\"other\")` without raising.\n- [ ] Parent receive/unpickling failures return `RunResult(abstain_reason=\"other\")` without raising.\n- [ ] Timeout, large-result drain, exception, signal-crash, cleanup, and reap-lag contracts remain green under spawn.\n- [ ] The documented public contract states importability/pickleability requirements and the explicit fork risk.\n- [ ] Focused grounding tests, lint, typecheck, and repository tests pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787025341424785001,"uuid":"264a49fb-41ef-4ca6-a7b8-23b28f06b50b"}